The env_0079_property_restoration_contractor scenario is delivered, with N=5 difficulties and M=2 tasks each, 10 tasks in all. All three delivery conditions hold, and I re-ran every check myself at the end:

- **Final load check:** `validate_scenario` returns VALID, with all 10 tasks loading, 62 tools, 355 documents and no warnings.
- **Policy audits:** every difficulty's final verdict is PASS / PASS / charter CLEAN, and all 7 instantiation gates plus the traceability check are green.
- **KB audits:** every difficulty's final KB verdict is PASS / PASS / KB CLEAN.
- **Blueprint:** unchanged since it was frozen; `check_blueprint` still says BLUEPRINT OK.
- **Identifiers:** no customer name, phone, email or reference number repeats across difficulties.

The company in the blueprint is Ridgecrest Restoration & Reconstruction, which has seven product lines. Fire & Smoke Mitigation and the commercial/property-manager service agreements are not claimed by any difficulty. They were rendered but, as the pipeline intends, never audited.

| Difficulty | Product | Policy audit rounds | KB audit rounds | Docs |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| water_mitigation_billing | water | 6 | 3 | 65 |
| mold_remediation_jobs | mold | 4 | 3 | 56 |
| rebuild_contracts_and_draws | rebuild | 15 | 2 | 55 |
| contents_packout_and_storage | contents | 8 | 4 | 75 |
| insurance_claim_services | claims | 10 | 4 | 66 |
| (not claimed) | fire, account | no audit | no audit | 21, 17 |

**Open items I left in place:**
- **Mold KB note S2:** the frozen base mold data still lists tier unit rates for three lines whose pricing rule the extended policies retire. The published docs settle it line by line and no scored value moves, so I logged it rather than reopening the loop.
- **Rebuild:** a seeded claim file shows a deductible due with no assessment row behind it. No scored step reads that row, and the gates reject seeding rows nothing reads, so it stays as accepted residue.
- **Rebuild:** one policy restates the base rule that work resumes and a remobilization fee is booked once a draw is paid, but no tool in that difficulty can record either. No task world reaches that case; logged as a known blueprint issue.
- **Frozen base text:** the fire, account and rebuild charters have wording defects (missing day-count conventions, a stale parameter description, an ambiguous rebate base). None affects a task, so they render as written and are logged.
- **Legal citations:** the blueprint agent cited the FTC Cooling-Off Rule, Florida's 2023 assignment-of-benefits ban, Texas Insurance Code ch. 707, EPA's lead-paint renovation rule and the Texas/New York mold licensing split from memory. I checked them against my own knowledge only, not a primary source.

Rebuild needed 15 policy rounds because the reworker's fixes kept introducing new defects. Two loops closed only after I gave explicit routes; I added each to `audits/render_source/realism_bar.md` (RULE-1 to RULE-7) so both reworkers and auditors could see them.

Every launch, result and decision is in `env/env_0079_property_restoration_contractor/worklog.md`, which ends with the DELIVERED line. I also saved this run's lessons to memory for later runs.
